  "response": "그날 밤, 혼자서 그 사실을 마주했을 때의 무서움이 여기까지 전해지는 것 같아요. 서른한 살이라는 나이가, 뭘 좋아하는지 모른다는 사실과 만나니까 더 날카로웠던 것 같고요.\n\n그런데 한 가지는 눈에 띄어요. \"당신 생각은 대체 뭐야?\"라는 말에 머릿속이 하얘지셨다고 하셨잖아요. 그런데 지금 이 자리에서, 어머니한테 물어보는 패턴을 스스로 알아채셨고, 그걸 무섭다고 느끼셨고, 여기까지 오셨어요. 그건 분명히 '생각'이에요. 다만 그 생각이平时에는 어머니의 답변 뒤에 숨어 있어서, 그걸 꺼내야 하는 순간에 손에 잡히지 않았던 건지도 모르겠어요.\n\n그날 밤 이후로, 혹시 \"이건 내가 진짜 원하는 건데\" 하고 느껴본 순간이 있었을까요? 아주 사소한 거라도요.",
  "reasoning": "The user is presenting a counseling dialogue. The client has just shared something quite vulnerable - they came to counseling because their fiancé said they can't get married until this is resolved. The core issue seems to be around identity and autonomy - they realized they don't know what they like or think, they rely heavily on their mother for decisions, and their fiancé's question \"What is YOUR opinion?\" left them completely blank. They expressed fear about being 31 and not knowing themselves.\n\nWhat the client needs right now:\n- They've just made a significant self-disclosure and expressed fear. This is a moment of vulnerability.\n- They don't need advice or solutions yet. They need to feel heard and that what they shared makes sense.\n- They've actually answered the counselor's initial question (what do you want to talk about) - they came because of the fiancé's ultimatum, but the deeper issue they identified is the fear of not knowing themselves.\n- I should acknowledge the courage it took to share this, validate that the fear is understandable, and perhaps gently reflect back what they've identified as the core of their struggle.\n- I should NOT jump to solutions, NOT minimize (\"it'll be okay\"), NOT ask too many questions.\n\nLet me craft a response that:\n1. Acknowledges the difficulty of the situation they described\n2. Validates the fear without being dismissive\n3. Reflects back what they've identified - the gap between their age and their sense of self\n4. Maybe gently names what seems to be happening (the relationship with mother, the fiancé's question as a mirror)\n5. Perhaps one gentle question or invitation to explore further\n\nI want to be warm but not overly effusive. The client is clearly articulate and self-aware - they've already done significant reflection. I should meet them at that level.\n",
  "started_at": "2026-11-07T11:06:01.073496+00:00",
